course: dictionary
lesson: 1851
title: Cocoa: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which meaning the writer wants. «Cocoa» is a good example. It can mean the brown powder, the hot drink, or the beans that grow on a tree. Look for the clues.
explain: «Cocoa pods grow straight out of the trunk of the cacao tree» tells you that cocoa is the bean inside a plant part. «A cup of cocoa» tells you it is the hot drink, because you drink from a cup. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence?
explain: Cocoa is an uncountable noun, so you say «some cocoa», not «two cocoas». People sometimes say «a cocoa» to mean one cup of the drink, just as «a tea» means one cup of tea. The sentence clues will tell you which meaning is meant.
fact: Cocoa is a brown powder made from roasted cacao beans.
fact: Cocoa is also a hot drink made with milk or water, also called hot chocolate.
fact: Cocoa beans grow in pods on the cacao tree in hot tropical countries.
fact: «Cocoa butter» and «cocoa powder» are phrases where cocoa is an ingredient.
fact: «Chocolate is made from the seeds of the cocoa tree.» The seeds of the tree are the cocoa beans.
exercise: «That is why your hot cocoa cools on the table.» In this sentence, what is cocoa? | A tropical country | A tree with white pods | A pan for baking | *A hot drink
exercise: «Cocoa pods grow straight out of the trunk of the cacao tree.» What does the word grow tell you about cocoa here? | It is a sweet you can unwrap | It is a powder sold in a tin | It is a drink served in a cup | *It is a bean that grows on a plant
exercise: Ella says, «Can I have a cocoa?» What does she want? | *A cup of the hot drink | A cacao tree to plant | A bag of powder from the shop | A bar of chocolate to eat
test: «Cocoa beans grow in pods on the cacao tree.» Where do cocoa beans grow? | In a fridge | *On a tree in hot countries | Under the sea | Inside a cup
test: «The Aztecs used cocoa beans as money.» What does this tell you about cocoa beans? | They were tiny stones used for games | They were only eaten by children | They were kept in cold water | *They were valuable, so people used them to buy things
exam: «Chocolate is made from the seeds of the cocoa tree.» Which meaning of cocoa is used here? | A bitter juice from a fruit | A spicy sauce for meat | *The tree whose seeds make chocolate | A cup of hot drink with milk
